+  evidence:
+  - source: "eip.md"
+    locator: "Specification > Parameters; New-account surcharge; Intrinsic gas computation"
+    summary: "Changes TX_BASE_COST from 21,000 to 6,000 and adds a 25,000-gas, state-dependent surcharge for qualifying value transfers to non-existent accounts."
+  - source: "supporting/eip-2930.md"
+    locator: "Specification, paragraph beginning “At the beginning of execution”"
+    summary: "The pre-change access-list transaction intrinsic calculation uses the existing 21,000 base, showing the mechanism being replaced."
+  rationale: "A new state-dependent intrinsic-gas component is introduced while the existing base-cost mechanism is changed for every transaction type. Both changes alter existing gas accounting paths and their tests, matching score 3."
+  confidence: high
+  uncertainty_note: "The proposal’s statement that CREATE transactions are “unchanged” is ambiguous relative to the universal TX_BASE_COST replacement, but it does not change the presence or breadth of the gas-rule change."
+  exceptional_score_justification: null
